1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,520
This is Lain Zip, a research prototype using Apertus.

2
00:00:04,470 --> 00:00:11,155
It asks a practical question: when an agent remembers an error, can it check and revise
that memory?

3
00:00:12,108 --> 00:00:15,006
Here is an actual archived error.

4
00:00:14,956 --> 00:00:23,272
At the fixed input v equals zero, separate Apertus calls identify zero on the left and a
positive value on the right.

5
00:00:24,236 --> 00:00:27,977
The model retracts the note and writes a replacement.

6
00:00:27,927 --> 00:00:31,976
An exact polynomial auditor checks the expression.

7
00:00:31,976 --> 00:00:35,848
We preserve the original and save the checked revision.

8
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:41,159
On the later task, the old note leads to a wrong answer.

9
00:00:41,109 --> 00:00:44,519
The revised note restores the correct answer.

10
00:00:44,519 --> 00:00:47,834
The no note baseline was already correct.

11
00:00:48,804 --> 00:00:53,781
The frozen pilot completes three of four strict repair workflows.

12
00:00:53,731 --> 00:00:56,122
This is a narrow result.

13
00:00:56,122 --> 00:01:02,400
Two repaired errors repeat one task, and a newer test also shows a false withdrawal.

14
00:01:03,356 --> 00:01:07,138
Separate local training changes a small adapter.

15
00:01:07,088 --> 00:01:13,039
Periodic route success mass improves, but the final checkpoint advantage is small.

16
00:01:13,039 --> 00:01:17,033
These probabilities are not measured answer accuracy.

17
00:01:18,004 --> 00:01:23,538
Four selector batches favor training, while written summaries have mixed effects.

18
00:01:23,488 --> 00:01:26,885
A separate controller learns only withdrawal.

19
00:01:26,885 --> 00:01:30,567
We report that failure alongside the progress.

20
00:01:31,524 --> 00:01:38,960
The public submission includes a runnable prototype, raw evidence, training source and
seven adapters.

21
00:01:38,910 --> 00:01:44,929
Inspect the records, reproduce the checks, and help test useful memory revision.
